                                                            PROJECT REPORT – 5
                                            Healthcare Management System Using Agile Methodology
1. Introduction

The Healthcare Management System is a web-based application designed to manage healthcare services digitally. It helps hospitals and clinics maintain patient records, schedule appointments, and manage medical data efficiently, improving overall healthcare service delivery.

This project is developed using the Agile Methodology, which allows continuous improvement, flexibility, and faster delivery of healthcare-related features.

2. Problem Statement

Traditional healthcare systems often rely on paper-based records and manual processes, which can lead to data loss, delays, and errors in patient management. Doctors and staff face difficulties in accessing patient information quickly. There is a need for an automated healthcare system that ensures accurate, secure, and efficient data handling.

3. Objectives of the Project

To automate patient record management
To improve appointment scheduling
To reduce paperwork and manual errors
To ensure secure storage of medical data
To enhance healthcare service efficiency

4. Scope of the Project

The system supports patient registration, appointment booking, medical record management, and basic reporting. Administrators can manage doctors, patients, and system data, while doctors can view patient history and update medical records.

5. Agile Methodology

Agile methodology focuses on iterative development, continuous feedback, and adaptability. The healthcare system is developed in multiple sprints, with each sprint delivering functional healthcare modules.

Agile Practices Followed

Incremental development
Continuous testing
Regular stakeholder feedback
Adaptive planning

